an></span></strong><span><span><span><span> Marzen<br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Sierra Nevada Oktoberfest</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> Festbier<br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Port City Oktoberfest</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> Marzen<br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Silver Branch Oktoberfest</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> Marzen<br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Hofbrau Oktoberfestbier</span></span></span></span></strong></p></figcaption></figure><figure><img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/442967cf-2944-aa6d-dde1-99f0046f997d.jpeg\" width=\"298\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><p><span><span><span><span>🎃 Pumpkin Party<br></span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>• Kentucky Pumpkin Barrel Ale</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span><br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Alewerks Pumpkin</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> Ale<br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Shipyard Smashed Pumpkin</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> Imperial Ale<br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Shipyard NA Pumpkinhead</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span><br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Solace Air Gourd’n</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> Pumpkin Porter</span></span></span></span></p></figcaption></figure></div>\n<div class=\"reader-image-row reader-brew-grid\" data-columns=\"2\"><figure><img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/bcf9f3b5-755b-d429-df2c-db66c0a398ed.jpeg\" width=\"298\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><p><span><span><span><span>🍎 Fall Ciders<br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>1911 Donut</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> Cider<br>•</span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span> Blake’s Cider Mill Donut</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span><br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Ace Pumpkin </span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span>Cider</span></span></span></span></p></figcaption></figure><figure><img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/09a9abc9-821a-12e0-56d5-076450f0ccb3.jpeg\" width=\"298\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><p><span><span><span><span>🦉 Even more pumpkin from </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Elysian</span></span></span></span></strong></p>\n<p><span><span><span><span>•</span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span> Night Owl </span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span>Pumpkin Ale<br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Pumpkin Pack</span></span></span></span></strong></p>\n<p>Bluejacket / Schilling / Eggenberg Artus Vienna Lager</p></figcaption></figure></div>\n<img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/edc87471-2940-664d-9574-e6e0a98d711b.jpeg\" width=\"520\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\">\n<p><span><span><span>You know that thing where your friend gives you a piece of advice or tells you to try something and you just completely ignore them, even when they insist? They keep giving the same advice / recommending this same thing, and you keep ignoring them, but actually your brain is holding onto it and you're internalizing it without realizing it? Then one day, you find yourself doing / trying the thing they advised / recommended and you think \"Wow I've just discovered this very cool thing!\" Of course later you will realize, (or your friend will point out,) that it was all their idea in the first place and you will be forced to admit they were right. Well, Greek whites are that thing for me. Beth has been touting Greek whites directly into my face for some time now. For some reason, and to my detriment, I've been holding back on Greek whites. But no more.</span></span></span></p>\n<p><span><span><span>Our newest Greek white wine to hit the shelves is the </span></span></span><strong><span><span><span>Orealios Robola</span></span></span></strong><span><span><span>. Made from 100% Robola grape, this is not the Assyrtiko you're probably used to seeing when it comes to Greek whites. Both of those grapes are known for producing dry, high acid, mineral-forward wines, but Robola plays second fiddle to Assyrtiko in terms of popularity and production volume. (We do </span><span>have some great Assyrtiko on the shelves here, and you should try that too!). Hailing from the Greek island of Kefalonia - which it has been argued is possibly the actual location of Homer's Ithaca, and yes, I did see The Odyssey last weekend - Orealios is a winery created by a co-op of growers who came together to build the winery. All organic and hand harvested, the project is truly led by the people who are closest to the grapes themselves. The juice is light, bright, and coastal. White grape dominates the flavor profile but there's some lovely salinity, lemon, and a touch of texture from lees aging. Honestly, this is super super easy to drink and the very best kind of crusher. Yes, it will go great in your Owala while you're watching The Odyssey. It's also perfect for seafood. And it does fine as a \"yeah, you were right\" glass with a friend as well. </span></span></span></p>\n<p><em><span><span><span><span>This week’s writeup is brought to you by Julie</span></span></span></span></em></p>\n<img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/c74c8ccc-1842-8f19-1ea4-35e3d6b44646.png\" width=\"534\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\">\n<p><span><span><span><span>The </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>FREE local contest </span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span>for the </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>DC State Fair</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> returns! This is a non-BJCP event and truly one of the most fun contests you’ll enter all year. Make something the committee finds tasty and win! There are categories for both Beer and Cider and there's still time to brew and get your entries in by August 21st. Open to all residents of DC and surrounding counties.</span></span></span></span></p>\n<img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/ee114eb5-8f0d-9c75-610a-7cf185e13f8a.png\" width=\"520\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\">\n<p>Thanks for your business! See you soon, Beth, Julie &amp; Aidan and the entire Brew Crew</p>",
